     2| * IVX Tool Engine — unified tool orchestration layer.
     3| *
     4| * Exposes 16 named tools that IVX can call directly, without Rork:
     5| *
     6| *   github.read           — Read repo info, branches, commits
     7| *   github.write          — Push file changes via GitHub API
     8| *   github.commit         — Create a commit with specified files
     9| *   github.workflow       — List workflows and recent runs
    10| *   render.status         — Get Render service + deploy status
    11| *   render.deploy         — Trigger a new Render deploy
    12| *   render.logs           — Get recent Render deploy logs
    13| *   render.rollback       — Rollback to a previous deploy
    14| *   supabase.audit        — Full Supabase audit (tables, auth, policies)
    15| *   supabase.migrate      — Run SQL migration on Supabase
    16| *   supabase.read_write_test — Read/write test against Supabase
    17| *   production.health     — Test production /health endpoint
    18| *   production.version    — Test production /version endpoint
    19| *   production.qa         — Run full QA suite against production
    20| *   commit.match          — Compare GitHub/Render/Production SHAs
    21| *   evidence.archive      — Generate and archive full evidence report
    22| *
    23| * Every tool returns { ok, error, ...data } — no secrets, no placeholders.
    24| * Tools that need credentials read them through the IVX Secure Vault.
